# Two equal Arrays holding Null (or Maps, or Bools) are `==`, yet `<=`
# between them raises "Type Null is not orderable", while `[1, null] <
# [2, null]` is true because ordering stops at the first difference. Whether
# an unorderable element raises thus depends on whether an earlier element
# differs. Unclear which is intended; this expectation assumes equal Arrays
# order as equal (the prefix up to the first unequal element decides, as
# with `==`), so `<=` and `>=` are true and `<` is false.
#= {
#=     result: [true, true, false, true],
#=     inputs: {a: [null], b: [null], m: [{}]},
#=     known_issue: 'FROST-154',
#= }
[a <= b, a >= b, a < b, m <= [{}]]
